# Brake - the leaving track is stopped like a hand on the platter, then the new one is in.
#
# The pitch falls with the speed, because that fall *is* the sound; correcting it would
# leave a track that quietly slows down, which is not a brake at all. The stop takes about
# an eighth of the span, so at a fifteen-second setting it is a couple of seconds - any
# longer and it stops sounding deliberate.

name    Brake
note    stops the leaving track dead, then drops the new one in
align   beat
tempo   free
power   free

lane out gain
    at 0.0    1.0    hold
    at 0.62   1.0    smooth
    at 0.75   0.0    hold
    at 1.0    0.0    hold

# 1.0 is the track's own speed; 0.05 is as slow as mpv will play rather than stall.
lane out speed
    at 0.0    1.0    hold
    at 0.62   1.0    smooth
    at 0.75   0.05   hold
    at 1.0    0.05   hold

lane in gain
    at 0.0    0.0    hold
    at 0.75   1.0    hold
    at 1.0    1.0    hold

hook at 0.62   toast brake
